<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000517> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Act of Communication by Movement of Information Bearing Artifact"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000517> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000402> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000517> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An Act of Communication in which some Material Artifact is used to transfer an Information Bearing Entity from sender(s) to receiver(s)."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000517> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "An Act of Communication by Movement of Information Bearing Artifact is distinguished by the fact that the Information Content Entity is transferred in virtue of its Information Bearing Artifact being transferred; as opposed to a new copy of the Information Content Entity being created in another bearer. Additional examples include passing notes in class, going door-to-door distributing pamphlets, lending/borrowing your physical copy of a book, etc."@en .
