<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Oscillation Process"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000004> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Oscillation"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Change in which the dependent entity alternates between two or more stases."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Oscillation is often thought of in the sense of motion, e.g., a swinging clock pendulum. However, the repetitive variation in location around a central point is technically a process of vibration, sometimes referred to as mechanical oscillation. Use the term Vibration Motion for those cases."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001754> "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Oscillation&oldid=1002978272"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000644> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/EventOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
