<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001691> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GMT-6"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001691> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "CST"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001691> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Central Standard Time"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001691> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/InformationEntityOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001692> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001692> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001328> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001692> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unix Time"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001692> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Unix Time is a Temporal Reference System for describing a point in time, defined as the number of seconds that have elapsed since 00:00:00 Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) Thursday, 1 January 1970 minus the number of leap seconds that have taken place since then.
(See: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time)"""@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001692> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/InformationEntityOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001693> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001693> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001235> .
